# Field reports and audits from real apps built on aio. They name the app, its
# internals and — for a security audit — exactly where its secrets were
# reachable. A private app's details must never leave this machine, so both
# directories are ignored AND `scripts/check-report-dirs.ts` refuses to let a
# file in either of them become tracked. `review/` was tracked for a month
# before anybody noticed, in a public repo and in the published package.
feedback/
review/
skills-lock.json
.openclaude-profile.json
.aio-test-home/
.aio-test-shards/
